+/// QLinearConv operator.
+///
+/// This performs a convolution on quantized inputs. The zero-point adjusted
+/// products `(x - x_zero_point) * (w - w_zero_point)` are accumulated in int32,
+/// an optional int32 bias with one value per output channel is added, and the
+/// result is requantized to the output type as
+/// `saturate(round_ties_even(acc * x_scale * w_scale / y_scale) + y_zero_point)`.
+///
+/// The input and output scales and zero points must be per-tensor (scalar or
+/// single-element vectors). The weight scale and zero point must have matching
+/// granularity: either both per-tensor or both per-channel, with one entry per
+/// output channel.
+///
+/// The output type is given by the type of the `y_zero_point` input, or
+/// defaults to u8 if it is omitted.
+///
+/// See <https://onnx.ai/onnx/operators/onnx__QLinearConv.html>.
+#[derive(Clone, Debug)]
